g on actual classmates rather than an imaginary “everyone,” the team began to see the difference between a broad idea and a target audience. Some students cared about health, some cared about taste, some cared about price, and some cared about speed. These differences affected whether the snack cart would work.',
        'The case shows why entrepreneurs should define the customer before buying inventory. The clearer the audience, the easier it becomes to ask useful questions and avoid expensive assumptions.',
